{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfP5bZVz5RwebnZPtvRxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This question isn't covered by any docs in this directory (the graphify graph is for this repo's own code, unrelated to your Supabase/pgvector project) — I don't have a source file to cite here.\n\nQuick diagnosis anyway: SSL read timeout on `.rpc()` at ~250K rows almost always means the query itself is slow, not a network issue. With `ivfflat` and `lists = 100`, recall/speed degrades as the table grows past the row count the index was tuned for — you likely need `lists` closer to `sqrt(N)` (~500 for 250K, more as you approach 650K), and you should `REINDEX` after bulk loads since ivfflat doesn't rebalance incrementally. Also increase the client timeout (`httpx.Timeout`) and consider switching to an `hnsw` index if you're on pgvector 0.5+, since it scales better than ivfflat at this row count."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":15947,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":839},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca0d8438-33bc-48d0-a610-7e87c164d02a","uuid":"93d29d00-d05d-4fc5-bed6-a09b55a6e433","timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:48:49.688Z","request_id":"req_011CfP5bZ4vc1dCE1PKNt1gC"}
